We clustered all computed similarity matrices using the Leiden algorithm and tested three values for the resolution parameter $\gamma$: the median ($Q_2$) of the respective similarity distribution, the third quartile ($Q_3$), and the average of the two ($\langle Q \rangle_{2,3}$).
Since the true pulling directions are known, we assess the clustering quality using normalized mutual information (NMI) scores. The results are summarized in Fig.~\ref{fig:Stb_panel2}A, comparing NMI scores for different similarity measures with varying data preprocessing and displaying Sankey diagrams for the highest NMI score results for each measure. Small clusters with five or fewer members are grouped together into a ''?'' cluster.  
