\section{Performance profiling of major computational kernels}
\label{sec:performance_profiling}

Having established how the two views of \code{BQRRP\_CPU} and \code{BQRRP\_GPU} are constructed, in \cref{sec:bqrrp_practical,sec:bqrrp_gpu}, it is important to analyze how different parts of these algorithms affect the overall algorithm performance, in order to identify the bottlenecks for future optimization.
In this section, we omit depicting the results for matrices with dimensions that are multiples of ten, as their performance profiling plots are nearly identical to those for matrices with dimensions that are powers of two.

\paragraph{CPU performance breakdown.} 
We first present in \cref{fig:cpu_runtime_breakdown} the algorithm runtime breakdown results for the two CPU versions of \code{BQRRP}.
We depict the percentage of runtime that is occupied by a given
component kernel of the two versions of \code{BQRRP\_CPU} on the $y$-axis.
We use square test matrices with $65{,}536$ rows and columns and the block size parameter $b$ varying as powers of two from $256$ to $2048$ ($x$-axis). 

