\paragraph{GPU performance breakdown.}
In \cref{fig:gpu_runtime_breakdown}, we present the runtime breakdown of the two implicit versions of \code{BQRRP\_GPU} to see any bottlenecks in their respective subroutines.
Any given implementation of \code{BQRRP\_GPU} uses a single GPU stream, and hence timing its computational kernels does not involve any complications.
We depict the percentage of runtime that is occupied by a given subcomponent of \code{BQRRP\_GPU} on the $y$-axis.
We use a square test matrix with $32{,}768$ rows and columns and the block size parameter $b$ varying as powers of two from $32$ to $2048$ ($x$-axis).

\begin{figure}[htp]
