with some $\beta \in (0,1)$, $k\in\mathbb{R}$ and $\mathcal{K} >0$. Then for any $\xi \in (0,1)$ and any $\nu\in (0,1)$ there exists $\bar{x} \in K_{r}(y)$ and $\delta=\delta(N) \in (0,1)$ such that
