\section{Case studies}
\label{sec:case}
This section demonstrates pooling effect for different rating criteria by using two standard financial products: collateralized loan obligations (CLOs) and catastrophe (CAT)
bonds. For CLOs, we compare scenario‐based rating criteria; for CAT bonds, whose losses are largely uncorrelated with macroeconomic performance, we compare law‐invariant rating criteria. We use both the risk measures and the corresponding credit ratings for demonstration. 

