\section*{Impact Statement}
To the best of our knowledge, this paper is the first to address the missing data problem, particularly missing not at random (MNAR), within the context of off-policy evaluation. Our approach has broad applicability to real-world domains such as healthcare, robotics, recommendation systems, and beyond. We believe that this work, along with the potential extensions discussed in Section \ref{eq:dm_extension} and Appendices, will inspire future research aimed at improving evaluation methods and decision-making in various machine learning applications.


