The new effective charges differ significantly from those previously established in the $fp$ shell. For example, effective charges of $e_\pi = 1.15e$, $e_\nu = 0.8e$ (ratio of 1.44) were determined for \isot{51}{Fe}/\isot{51}{Mn} at $N\approx Z$ in the $fp$ shell~\cite{duRietz2004}, and later updated to $e_\pi = 1.12e$, $e_\nu = 0.67e$ (ratio of 1.67) to best describe the stable $N=28$ and $Z=28$ chains~\cite{allmond2014}. The new values are also different from $e_\pi = 1.1e$, $e_\nu = 0.6e$ (ratio of 1.83) used recently to describe \isot{49,50}{Ti}~\cite{gray2024}. It has been argued that changes in the effective charges across the $fp$ shell are due to an isospin or orbital dependence~\cite{Valiente-Dobon2009}. However, it is worth noting that the previous and new effective charges all have similar sums, namely $e_\pi + e_\nu \approx 1.7e-1.95e$. 

