From Theorem \ref{secmaxEEG}, Lemmas \ref{geq3},\ref{C3ni},\ref{lemma 4.2} and \ref{lemma4.3}, we have the following result.
\begin{theorem}\label{unicyclicsecmax}
    Among the $k$-uniform unicyclic hypergraphs of order $n>3(k-1)$, the hypergraph $C_2(\dfrac{n}{k-1}-3,1)$ has the second largest Estrada index.
\end{theorem}
The following corollary is an immediate consequence of Theorems \ref{unicyclicmax} and \ref{unicyclicsecmax}.
\begin{corollary}
    Let $G^*$ be the $k$-uniform hypergraph with maximum Estrada index in $U(n)$ with diameter $d$. Then $G^*\cong C_2(\frac{n}{k-1}-2,0)$ if $d=2$, and $G^*\cong C_2(\frac{n}{k-1}-3,1)$ if $d=3$.
\end{corollary}
