	\begin{theorem*}
		All  $a^4b$-tilings  with  rational angles are the following:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item A one-parameter family of symmetric $a^4b$-pentagonal subdivisions of the tetrahedron with $12$ tiles (see the first picture of Figure \ref{poufen}).		
			\item A sequence of unique symmetric $a^4b$-pentagons with five angles $(\tfrac8f,\,1-\tfrac4f,\,1-\tfrac4f,\,\tfrac12+\tfrac2f,\,\tfrac12+\tfrac2f)\pi$ and		
