\underline{Theoretical Entropy Limit:}
\begin{itemize}
\item After 5000 time-steps, we separate out simulation 1, which carries on with the non-classical diffusion, from simulation 2, which now diffuses classically.
\item As per proposition \ref{diff_orb}, the off-diagonal sums are zero.
\item Therefore, per proposition \ref{stat_pts}, under the classical diffusion, the market density matrix will eventually diffuse to the maximum entropy state.
\item That is $S(\rho)\rightarrow\log(N)$, and $P_{ent}(\rho)\rightarrow 0$, as $T\rightarrow\infty$.
\item Figure \ref{frob_dist} shows the distance in the Frobenius norm, from the maximum entropy limit: $\rho=\frac{1}{N}\mathbb{I}$.
\item In both cases the reduced density matrix approaches the maximum entropy limit, but does so at a slower rate in the non-classical case.
\end{itemize}
