\subsection{Red House}

The Red House set-up included an STM32F103C8T6 microcontroller interfaced with an OLED display. The SCL pin of the OLED display is wired to port PB6 of the STM32 and the SDA pin is wired to port PB7. The Vcc pin of the OLED display is wired to the 3.3V supply of the STM32 and the GND pin is wired to the GND of the STM32. The OLED display is used to show the temperature and humidity readings as well as the distance of a detected obstacle from the gate, which it receives data from the Green House. Three LEDs are used to show the water level in the soil wired to ports PB1, PA7, and PA0 of the STM32, respectively. A buzzer connected to port PA4 is used to sound an alarm in the event of rainwater detection.

