\section{Gravitational moments}
\label{app:J2J4}

Our Uranus models presented in Sec.~\ref{subsec:uranus} showed that hydrogen-water demixing can redistribute material through the planet evolution. This redistribution of material can change the internal density distribution and consequently affect the calculated gravitational moments. We calculated the gravitational moments ($J_2$, $J_4$) of our Uranus models using the Theory of Figures of order 7 implemented by \citet{morf2024}. The results are shown in Fig.~\ref{figure:J2J4}. In the case with $T_{\rm offset}=600~$K, where the outer 2\% by mass are totally depleted in water, $J_2$ changes by about 200~ppm and $J_4$ by about 5~ppm. In the case with $T_{\rm offset}=1100~$K, where the outer 16\% by mass are totally depleted in water, $J_2$ changes by about 1000~ppm and $J_4$ by about 10~ppm. This shows the importance of considering hydrogen-water immiscibility in interior models that try to match the gravity data.

